  "stem": "Two trains A and B travelling on the same track are approaching each other with equal speeds of 40 m/s. The drivers of the trains begin to decelerate simultaneously when they are just 2.0 km apart. Assuming the decelerations of A is half that of B, what must be the minimum value of the deceleration of A to barely avoid collision?",
  "options": {
    "A": "3 m/s<sup>2</sup>",
    "B": "0.6 m/s<sup>2</sup>",
    "C": "1.2 m/s<sup>2</sup>",
    "D": "2.4 m/s<sup>2</sup>"
  },
  "answer": {
